      "writtenOn": "2020-12-10T00:02:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Encrypted by virtue of the full-disk encryption, and access guarded by virtue of SElinux.\n\nEffectively this conversion must always happen in a try/catch block, but that was already necessary because of I/O. And given that the same entity (system server) reads/writes this (minus a rooted user, but then all bets are off), the values should always be valid.\n\nGiven that this is not mainline, rollback is not an issue, and as for upgrading, we\u0027ll always have support the current set of capabilities anyways.",
